  "title": "Sol Plaatje",
  "summary": "Solomon Tshekisho Plaatje, born in 1876 in the Orange Free State, was a court interpreter, newspaper editor and writer. He was the first Secretary-General of the South African Native National Congress, formed in 1912, and in Native Life in South Africa (1916) he attacked the 1913 Land Act. He died on 19 June 1932.",
